License: Wolf4SDL's code from Wolfenstein 3D is offered under id Software's
license or the GNU GPL version 2, at the user's choice (its README.TXT,
"Licenses"). This port takes the GPL: LICENSE-GPL-2.0 is upstream's
license-gpl.txt, unchanged.

Taken: the engine's sources, id_*.c/h and wl_*.c/h with version.h,
foreign.h, f_spear.h, the audio*.h and gfxv_*.h headers, wolfpal.inc and
sodpal.inc. Files not listed below are unchanged.

Left out: signon.c (the sign-on picture as a 64000-byte initializer, too big
for tcc to compile on the board), the OPL2 emulators (mame/, dosbox/), the
SDL_mixer sound code and the platform ports and project files.

Replaced:
- id_sd.c: a sound manager with the same interface that plays nothing (the
  board has no sound output).

Changed (each says how at the top):
- id_ca.c, id_ca.h, id_pm.c: graphics chunks and VSWAP pages are read when
  used instead of all at startup, which needed 1.2 MB the board doesn't have.
  Other files read graphics chunks through CA_GrSeg instead of grsegs[]
  (id_vh.c, wl_game.c, wl_inter.c, wl_main.c, wl_menu.c, wl_text.c).
- id_vh.c, id_vh.h, id_vl.c, wl_draw.c, wl_scale.c, wl_play.c: the screen
  goes to xwolf.c, which sends it to an X server; the 3D view and sprites
  are drawn there from textures the server keeps, not into the 8-bit buffer.
  320x200, fades in one step, flashes as a tint.
- wl_def.h: packing only where a file format needs it (ARM wants the
  state tables' function pointers aligned); itoa and ltoa read the length of
  an uninitialized buffer, so numbers came out cut short ("100%" as "1%").
- wl_state.c: a left shift of a negative number, which C leaves undefined,
  is now a multiplication.
- wl_main.c, wl_game.c: no SDL_syswm or SDL_mixer headers.
- version.h: set up for the shareware data, version 1.4.

Added (MIT): xwolf.c and SDL.h (the SDL calls the engine makes, on X11
through ../demos/x11.h), build.sh, fetch-shareware.sh.

Game data is not included: fetch-shareware.sh downloads the shareware.
